/* Tekrar havuzu: rd-restatement, rd-completion, rd-irrelevant */
PRACTICE.push(
  /* ---------- rd-restatement ---------- */
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-01", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-10","w7-12"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Few economists would deny that access to affordable credit has played a major role in the growth of small businesses in emerging economies.”", o:["Most economists accept that affordable credit has contributed significantly to the expansion of small businesses in emerging economies.","Few economists have examined how affordable credit affects small businesses in emerging economies.","Economists increasingly deny that credit plays any role in the growth of small businesses in emerging economies.","According to most economists, small businesses in emerging economies have grown despite the lack of affordable credit.","Some economists claim that affordable credit has slowed the growth of small businesses in emerging economies."], a:0, e:"“Few … would deny” = neredeyse hiçbiri inkâr etmez, yani çoğu kabul eder; “a major role” = “contributed significantly”. B “Few economists” ifadesini aynen tekrarlar ama fiili “examine” yaparak anlamı tamamen değiştirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-02", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-11","w7-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Had it not been for the construction of extensive irrigation canals, the ancient cities of Mesopotamia could never have supported such large populations.”", o:["The ancient cities of Mesopotamia built irrigation canals because their populations had already become too large.","Despite their irrigation canals, the ancient cities of Mesopotamia were unable to support large populations.","The large populations of Mesopotamian cities were supported mainly by trade rather than by irrigation.","It was the extensive irrigation canals that made it possible for the ancient cities of Mesopotamia to sustain such large populations.","If the ancient cities of Mesopotamia had built irrigation canals, they could have supported larger populations."], a:3, e:"“Had it not been for X” = X olmasaydı; gerçekte kanallar yapılmıştır ve kalabalık nüfus onlar sayesinde mümkün olmuştur. E aynı kelimeleri kullanır ama gerçekleşmiş durumu (kanalların yapılması) gerçekleşmemiş gibi sunar."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-03", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-12","w7-11"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The more densely a city is populated, the more quickly infectious diseases tend to spread within it.”", o:["Infectious diseases always spread quickly in cities, regardless of how densely they are populated.","Infectious diseases generally spread faster in cities with higher population densities.","Cities become more densely populated as infectious diseases spread within them.","A densely populated city is certain to suffer from an outbreak of infectious disease.","Infectious diseases spread more slowly in cities than in rural areas."], a:1, e:"“The more …, the more quickly … tend to” orantılı ve eğilim bildiren bir ilişkidir: nüfus yoğunluğu arttıkça hastalık daha hızlı yayılır. C sebep ile sonucun yerini değiştirir; D ise “tend to” eğilimini “certain” kesinliğine çevirerek abartır."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-04", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-07","reading-11"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Not until the late nineteenth century were women admitted to most European universities on equal terms with men.”", o:["Women were admitted to most European universities on equal terms with men long before the late nineteenth century.","By the late nineteenth century, women had stopped applying to most European universities.","In the late nineteenth century, most European universities began to admit fewer women than men.","Women were admitted to most European universities in the late nineteenth century, but not on equal terms with men.","It was only in the late nineteenth century that most European universities began to accept women on the same basis as men."], a:4, e:"“Not until X were …” = ancak X'te gerçekleşti; bu, “It was only in … that” ile aynı zaman vurgusunu verir. A sıralamayı tersine çevirir; D ise “on equal terms” kısmını olumsuza çevirerek anlamı bozar."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-05", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-08"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The engineers could scarcely have anticipated that a bridge designed to last a century would need major repairs within twenty years.”", o:["The engineers expected from the start that the bridge would need major repairs within twenty years.","The engineers found it difficult to repair the bridge, which had been designed to last a century.","It was almost impossible for the engineers to foresee that a bridge meant to last a hundred years would require significant repairs after only two decades.","Although the bridge was designed to last a century, it has never needed any major repairs.","The engineers designed the bridge to last only twenty years, but it has survived for a century."], a:2, e:"“could scarcely have anticipated” = öngörmeleri neredeyse imkânsızdı; “within twenty years” = “after only two decades”. B “scarcely” sözcüğünü “onarmakta zorlanmak” gibi yorumlayarak öngörü anlamını kaybeder."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-06", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-09"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Much as solar power has become cheaper over the past decade, its share of global electricity generation remains relatively small.”", o:["Because solar power has become cheaper, it now generates most of the world's electricity.","Solar power has become cheaper precisely because its share of global electricity generation is small.","Although solar power costs much less than it did a decade ago, it still accounts for a fairly limited portion of the electricity generated worldwide.","As solar power has grown more expensive, its share of global electricity has decreased.","Solar power will remain a small share of global electricity until it becomes cheaper."], a:2, e:"“Much as” burada “although” anlamında zıtlık bildirir: ucuzlamasına rağmen payı hâlâ küçüktür. A “much as” yapısını sebep gibi okuyup sonucu da “most” diyerek tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-07", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-10","reading-11"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“But for the protective ozone layer, far more ultraviolet radiation would reach the Earth's surface, making life on land extremely difficult.”", o:["Without the ozone layer to protect it, the Earth's surface would receive much more ultraviolet radiation, which would make it very hard for life to exist on land.","The ozone layer allows ultraviolet radiation to reach the Earth's surface, which makes life on land difficult.","Life on land is extremely difficult because too much ultraviolet radiation reaches the Earth's surface.","Even if the ozone layer disappeared, life on land would easily adapt to higher levels of ultraviolet radiation.","Life on land became possible only after ultraviolet radiation had destroyed the ozone layer."], a:0, e:"“But for X” = “Without X” (X olmasaydı); cümle gerçek dışı bir durumu anlatır, gerçekte ozon tabakası korur. C bu gerçek dışı sonucu şu anki gerçek durum gibi sunar; B ise ozonun işlevini tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-08", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-12","reading-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Contrary to popular belief, camels do not store water in their humps; the humps are in fact made up mostly of fat.”", o:["As most people believe, camels store water in their humps, which also contain some fat.","Camels store both fat and water in their humps, contrary to what most people think.","It is widely believed that camels' humps contain fat, but they actually store water.","Camels' humps are made up mostly of water, although many people believe otherwise.","Although many people think that camels keep water in their humps, these humps actually consist largely of fat."], a:4, e:"“Contrary to popular belief” = pek çok kişi aksini düşünse de; hörgüçte su değil, çoğunlukla yağ vardır. C yaygın inanış ile gerçeği yer değiştirerek anlamı tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-09", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-10","w7-08"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“It is by no means certain that the new drug will prove as effective in older patients as it did in the clinical trials.”", o:["The new drug is certain to be less effective in older patients than it was in the clinical trials.","Whether the new drug will work as well in older patients as it did in the clinical trials is far from clear.","The clinical trials showed that the new drug is most effective in older patients.","The new drug proved ineffective in the clinical trials, especially among older patients.","There is no doubt that the new drug will be as effective in older patients as it was in the clinical trials."], a:1, e:"“by no means certain” = hiç de kesin değil, yani belirsiz; bu “far from clear” ile karşılanır. A belirsizliği “daha az etkili olacağı kesin” diyerek yeni bir kesinliğe çevirir; E ise anlamı tamamen tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-10", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-11","reading-12"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The less time teenagers spend on social media, the better they tend to sleep.”", o:["Teenagers spend less time on social media when they sleep better.","Teenagers who use social media will never be able to sleep well.","Social media has no measurable effect on the sleep of teenagers.","Teenagers who reduce the amount of time they spend on social media generally sleep better.","Teenagers sleep less as they spend less time on social media."], a:3, e:"“The less …, the better … tend to” = sosyal medyada daha az zaman geçiren gençler genellikle daha iyi uyur. A ilişkinin yönünü tersine çevirir (iyi uyku → az kullanım); B ise eğilimi “never” ile mutlak bir yargıya dönüştürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-11", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-07"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“It was not until satellite images became widely available that scientists could accurately measure the rate of Arctic ice loss.”", o:["Scientists measured Arctic ice loss accurately before satellite images became widely available.","Satellite images became widely available because scientists wanted to measure Arctic ice loss.","Even with widely available satellite images, scientists have been unable to measure Arctic ice loss accurately.","Only after satellite images had become widely available were scientists able to measure accurately how fast Arctic ice was disappearing.","Arctic ice loss slowed down once satellite images became widely available."], a:3, e:"“It was not until X that …” = ancak X'ten sonra; bu “Only after … were” yapısıyla aynı sıralamayı verir. A zaman sıralamasını tersine çevirir; B ise cümlede olmayan bir sebep-sonuç ilişkisi ekler."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-12", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-09"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“While the printing of paper money made trade easier in Song China, it also led to periods of severe inflation when too many notes were issued.”", o:["Because paper money caused severe inflation, it made trade more difficult in Song China.","In Song China, paper money facilitated trade, but issuing excessive amounts of it sometimes caused serious inflation.","Trade in Song China became easier only after inflation had been brought under control.","The printing of paper money in Song China never caused inflation, since the number of notes was strictly limited.","Song China issued too many notes because trade had become easier."], a:1, e:"“While” burada zıtlık bildirir: kâğıt para ticareti kolaylaştırdı ama fazla basıldığında enflasyona yol açtı. E “too many notes” ifadesini tekrar eder ama cümlede olmayan bir sebep (ticaretin kolaylaşması) ekler."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-13", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-07"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“No sooner had the company launched its new smartphone than customers began reporting problems with the battery.”", o:["Customers started to complain about battery problems almost immediately after the company launched its new smartphone.","The company launched its new smartphone only after it had solved the battery problems reported by customers.","Customers reported problems with the battery long before the company launched its new smartphone.","The company delayed the launch of its new smartphone because of battery problems.","Few customers had any problems with the battery of the company's new smartphone."], a:0, e:"“No sooner had … than” = … yapar yapmaz; şikâyetler lansmanın hemen ardından başlamıştır. C sıralamayı tersine çevirir; B ise sorunların lansmandan önce çözüldüğünü söyleyerek anlamı bozar."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-14", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-11","w7-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Should the current rate of deforestation continue, many species unique to the region may disappear within a few decades.”", o:["The current rate of deforestation has already caused many species unique to the region to disappear.","Many species unique to the region will certainly disappear within a few decades, whatever happens to deforestation.","If deforestation carries on at its present pace, numerous species found only in the region could die out in the coming decades.","Deforestation in the region will slow down within a few decades, allowing its unique species to recover.","Many species unique to the region have survived despite the current rate of deforestation."], a:2, e:"“Should X continue” = “If X continues”; “may disappear” bir olasılıktır. A olası bir gelecek sonucu gerçekleşmiş bir olay gibi sunar; B ise koşulu ortadan kaldırıp “certainly” ile kesinlik ekler."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-15", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-10","w7-08"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Hardly any of the manuscripts from the ancient library survived the fire.”", o:["Most of the manuscripts from the ancient library were saved from the fire.","The fire destroyed the ancient library only with great difficulty.","Several manuscripts from the ancient library were damaged, but none was lost in the fire.","The fire hardly damaged the manuscripts in the ancient library.","Almost all of the manuscripts in the ancient library were destroyed in the fire."], a:4, e:"“Hardly any … survived” = neredeyse hiçbiri kurtulmadı, yani neredeyse hepsi yok oldu. D “hardly” sözcüğünü tekrar eder ama onu “damaged” fiiline bağlayarak anlamı tam tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-16", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-12","reading-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The decline of the ancient port city was caused not so much by foreign invasions as by the gradual silting of its harbour.”", o:["Foreign invasions and the silting of its harbour contributed equally to the decline of the ancient port city.","Foreign invasions were the main reason for the decline of the ancient port city, although its harbour also silted up.","The harbour of the ancient port city silted up as a result of repeated foreign invasions.","The ancient port city declined neither because of foreign invasions nor because of the silting of its harbour.","The slow build-up of silt in its harbour, rather than foreign invasions, was the main cause of the ancient port city's decline."], a:4, e:"“not so much X as Y” = asıl neden X değil, Y'dir; yani limanın dolması ana nedendir. B iki nedenin önem sırasını tersine çevirir; A ise ikisini eşit gösterir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-17", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-12","w7-11"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The earlier a second language is learned, the more native-like the speaker's pronunciation is likely to be.”", o:["People who learn a second language late will never be able to pronounce it correctly.","Having native-like pronunciation makes it easier to learn a second language early.","Those who learn a second language at a younger age are more likely to develop native-like pronunciation.","Pronunciation is the only aspect of a language that is affected by the age at which it is learned.","Learning a second language early has little effect on how native-like one's pronunciation becomes."], a:2, e:"“The earlier …, the more … likely” orantılı bir olasılık ilişkisidir: erken öğrenen, ana dili gibi telaffuz etmeye daha yatkındır. A “likely” ifadesini “never” ile mutlak bir yargıya çevirir; B ise sebep ile sonucu yer değiştirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-18", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-10","reading-11"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“If it were not for tourism, many of the small villages on the island would have been abandoned long ago.”", o:["Tourism has caused many of the small villages on the island to be abandoned.","Many small villages on the island were abandoned long ago, before tourism began.","Despite tourism, many of the small villages on the island have been abandoned.","Tourism is the main reason why many of the island's small villages are still inhabited today.","The small villages on the island would attract more tourists if they had not been abandoned."], a:3, e:"“If it were not for X” = X olmasaydı; gerçekte turizm vardır ve köyler bu sayede hâlâ yaşamaktadır. C “abandoned” sözcüğünü tekrar eder ama gerçek dışı sonucu gerçekleşmiş gibi sunar; A ise ilişkiyi tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-19", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-09"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Even though antibiotics are ineffective against viruses, they are still frequently prescribed for common colds.”", o:["Antibiotics are often prescribed for common colds, despite having no effect on viruses.","Because antibiotics are effective against viruses, doctors often prescribe them for common colds.","Antibiotics are rarely prescribed for common colds since they cannot fight viruses.","Common colds are caused by bacteria, which is why antibiotics are frequently prescribed for them.","Doctors have stopped prescribing antibiotics for common colds because they are ineffective against viruses."], a:0, e:"“Even though” zıtlık bildirir: işe yaramamasına rağmen sık reçete edilir; “despite” aynı ilişkiyi korur. C mantıklı görünen bir sebep-sonuç kurar ama “frequently” ifadesini “rarely” ile tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-20", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-08","reading-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The findings of the study can hardly be regarded as conclusive, given the small number of participants involved.”", o:["The study involved few participants, but its findings are nonetheless conclusive.","Since only a small number of people took part in the study, its findings can scarcely be considered definitive.","The researchers had difficulty finding participants because the study's findings were inconclusive.","The study's findings are conclusive precisely because the number of participants was small.","The number of participants had no effect on how conclusive the findings of the study were."], a:1, e:"“can hardly be regarded as conclusive” = kesin sayılamaz; “given” burada gerekçe bildirir (“since”). C “hardly” anlamını “katılımcı bulmakta zorlanmak” gibi yorumlayıp sebep-sonucu tersine çevirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-21", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-07"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Only by reducing its dependence on imported fuel can the country hope to protect its economy from sudden rises in energy prices.”", o:["The country's economy is protected from sudden rises in energy prices because it imports large amounts of fuel.","The country can shield its economy from sharp increases in energy prices only if it relies less on fuel from abroad.","Reducing its dependence on imported fuel will have no effect on how the country's economy responds to energy prices.","The country has already reduced its dependence on imported fuel, so its economy is fully protected.","Sudden rises in energy prices have forced the country to import more fuel."], a:1, e:"“Only by X can …” = ancak X ile mümkündür, yani X bir ön koşuldur; bu “only if” ile karşılanır. D ön koşulu gerçekleşmiş bir olay gibi sunarak “fully protected” diye abartır."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-22", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-12","reading-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Far from being a modern invention, the idea of a universal basic income can be traced back to the sixteenth century.”", o:["The idea of a universal basic income was first proposed in modern times.","The idea of a universal basic income was popular in the sixteenth century but has since been forgotten.","A universal basic income was introduced in several countries in the sixteenth century.","Although the idea of a universal basic income is modern, it resembles some sixteenth-century practices.","The idea of a universal basic income is not a recent one; its origins go back as far as the sixteenth century."], a:4, e:"“Far from being X” = X olmak şöyle dursun, hiç de X değil; fikir yeni değildir, kökeni 16. yüzyıla uzanır. C “fikri” fiilen uygulanmış bir politikaya çevirir; A ve D ise fikri modern sayarak “Far from being” olumsuzlamasını gözden kaçırır."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-23", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“The signals from the distant galaxy are too faint to be detected by ordinary telescopes.”", o:["Ordinary telescopes can detect the signals from the distant galaxy, but only with some difficulty.","The signals from the distant galaxy are faint because ordinary telescopes cannot detect them.","Ordinary telescopes are unable to pick up the signals from the distant galaxy because the signals are so weak.","The signals from the distant galaxy are strong enough to be detected by ordinary telescopes.","Only a few ordinary telescopes have been used to detect the signals from the distant galaxy."], a:2, e:"“too faint to be detected” = algılanamayacak kadar zayıf; yani sıradan teleskoplar bu sinyalleri hiç algılayamaz. A algılamanın zorla da olsa mümkün olduğunu söyler; B ise sebep ile sonucu yer değiştirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-24", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-10","w7-12"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Not all experts agree that raising the minimum wage leads to higher unemployment.”", o:["No experts believe that raising the minimum wage leads to higher unemployment.","All experts agree that raising the minimum wage reduces unemployment.","Most experts have never studied the link between the minimum wage and unemployment.","Some experts do not accept the view that an increase in the minimum wage results in higher unemployment.","Experts agree that higher unemployment leads governments to raise the minimum wage."], a:3, e:"“Not all experts agree” = bazı uzmanlar katılmıyor; derece “some”dır. A bu kısmi olumsuzluğu “No experts” ile tümel olumsuzluğa çevirerek abartır."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-25", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-09"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Whereas earlier studies focused mainly on the genetic causes of obesity, recent research has paid more attention to environmental factors such as diet and sleep.”", o:["Recent research has concentrated more on environmental influences like diet and sleep, while earlier studies were largely concerned with the genetic causes of obesity.","Both earlier and recent studies have focused mainly on the genetic causes of obesity.","Earlier studies showed that diet and sleep are more important than genes in causing obesity.","Recent research has proved that obesity has no genetic causes.","Recent research focuses on genetic factors, whereas earlier studies examined diet and sleep."], a:0, e:"“Whereas” iki dönemi karşılaştırır: eski çalışmalar genetiğe, yenileri çevresel etkenlere odaklanır. E aynı karşılaştırma yapısını kullanır ama iki dönemin odağını yer değiştirir; D ise “no genetic causes” diyerek abartır."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-26", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["w7-08"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Judging by the tools found at the site, the settlement's inhabitants must have been skilled metalworkers.”", o:["The tools discovered at the site strongly suggest that the people who lived in the settlement were skilled at working with metal.","The inhabitants of the settlement were skilled metalworkers, so they must have made tools for other sites.","The tools found at the site were probably brought from elsewhere, since the inhabitants could not work metal.","The settlement's inhabitants should have learned metalworking from neighbouring communities.","Archaeologists are certain that no metal tools were used at the site."], a:0, e:"“must have been” geçmişe dair güçlü bir çıkarımdır ve dayanağı bulunan aletlerdir; A bunu “strongly suggest” ile aynı derecede verir. D “should have” ile çıkarımı “yapmaları gerekirdi” anlamına çevirir; B ise dayanak ile sonucun yerini değiştirir."},
  {id:"r-rd-restatement-27", sub:"rd-restatement", from:["reading-11","w7-10"], q:"Verilen cümleye anlamca en yakın cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n“Unless action is taken to reduce water consumption, the region could face severe shortages within the next decade.”", o:["The region is facing severe water shortages because it has already reduced its water consumption.","The region will face severe water shortages in the next decade, whatever measures are taken.","Reducing water consumption will cause severe shortages in the region within the next decade.","If steps are not taken to cut water consumption, serious water shortages may occur in the region in the coming decade.","The region has taken action to reduce water consumption, so shortages are no longer possible."], a:3, e:"“Unless” = “if … not”; “could face” bir olasılıktır. B koşulu ortadan kaldırıp sonucu kaçınılmaz gösterir; C ise önlem ile tehlike arasındaki ilişkiyi tersine çevirir."},

  /* ---------- rd-completion ---------- */
  {id:"r-rd-completion-01", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-01","reading-15"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nLightning is one of the few natural processes that can convert nitrogen in the atmosphere into a form that plants can use. The enormous heat of a lightning bolt breaks apart nitrogen molecules, allowing the atoms to combine with oxygen. ---- Once they reach the soil, they act as a natural fertiliser, supplying nutrients that help crops and wild plants grow.", o:["Thunderstorms are most frequent in tropical regions near the equator.","The resulting compounds dissolve in rainwater and are carried down to the ground.","Nitrogen makes up about seventy-eight percent of the Earth's atmosphere.","Farmers, therefore, no longer need to use artificial fertilisers.","Lightning can also cause dangerous forest fires during dry summers."], a:1, e:"Sonraki cümledeki “they” zamiri ve “reach the soil” ifadesi, havada oluşan bileşiklerin toprağa indiğini söyleyen bir ara cümle gerektirir; bunu yalnızca B sağlar. C azottan söz ettiği için ilgili görünür ama “they” zamirinin göndermesini karşılamaz."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-02", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-04"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nFor most of human history, maps were drawn with the mapmaker's own region at the centre. Chinese maps placed China in the middle, while medieval European maps often put Jerusalem at their heart. Even today, the most familiar world map in many countries, the Mercator projection, greatly enlarges regions far from the equator, making Europe and North America appear larger than they really are. ----", o:["The Mercator projection was originally designed for sailors in the sixteenth century.","Jerusalem was an important destination for pilgrims in the Middle Ages.","Therefore, all modern maps show the true size of every continent.","China was one of the first civilisations to produce paper.","Maps, in other words, reflect not only geography but also the perspective of the people who make them."], a:4, e:"Paragrafın her örneği haritaların çizenin bakış açısını yansıttığını gösterir; E bu örnekleri “in other words” ile genel bir sonuca bağlar. A Mercator kelimesini tekrar eder ama paragrafın düşüncesini ilerletmez; C ise son cümleyle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-03", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-03","reading-15"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n---- This phenomenon occurs because the brain tends to fill gaps in memory with information that seems plausible, even when it did not actually happen. In one well-known experiment, participants who had watched a film of a car accident gave higher estimates of the cars' speed when asked how fast they were going when they \"smashed\" into each other than when they \"hit\" each other.", o:["Human memory is surprisingly prone to distortion, and people can sincerely recall details of events that never took place.","Car accidents are one of the leading causes of death among young adults.","Films are often used in psychology experiments because they are easy to show to large groups.","The brain consists of billions of nerve cells connected by synapses.","In this experiment, however, most participants remembered the accident accurately."], a:0, e:"“This phenomenon” ifadesi ilk cümlede bir olgunun adlandırılmasını gerektirir; A hafızanın çarpıtılabildiğini söyleyerek bu göndermeyi karşılar. E “this experiment” derken henüz anlatılmamış bir deneye gönderme yapar ve sonraki bulguyla çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-04", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-02","reading-14"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nIn the early twentieth century, most astronomers believed that the Milky Way made up the entire universe. The fuzzy patches of light known as nebulae were thought to be clouds of gas within our own galaxy. ---- His measurements showed that one of these patches, the Andromeda nebula, was far too distant to be part of the Milky Way. Almost overnight, the known universe expanded to include countless other galaxies.", o:["Some nebulae are regions where new stars are being formed.","Consequently, astronomers stopped studying nebulae for several decades.","In 1924, however, the American astronomer Edwin Hubble used a powerful new telescope to measure the distance to several of these objects.","The Milky Way contains between one hundred and four hundred billion stars.","Astronomers therefore agreed that the Andromeda nebula lay inside our galaxy."], a:2, e:"Sonraki cümledeki “His measurements” bir kişiyi ve bir ölçümü gerektirir; “however” da eski görüşle karşıtlığı kurar. E “Andromeda” sözcüğünü tekrar eder ama sonraki cümlenin söylediğiyle doğrudan çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-05", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-01","w8-05"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nCities are often several degrees warmer than the surrounding countryside, a phenomenon known as the urban heat island effect. Materials such as asphalt and concrete absorb large amounts of heat during the day. ---- As a result, temperatures in city centres may remain high long after sunset, increasing energy demand for air conditioning and posing health risks during heatwaves.", o:["Many cities have introduced parks and green roofs to reduce temperatures.","Asphalt was first used to pave roads in the nineteenth century.","Rural areas, by contrast, tend to have fewer residents.","They then release this stored heat slowly throughout the night.","Air conditioning, in turn, has become cheaper in recent years."], a:3, e:"“As a result, … remain high long after sunset” sonucu, gündüz depolanan ısının gece yavaşça salındığını söyleyen bir neden cümlesi gerektirir; “They” de asfalt ve betona gönderme yapar. A konuyla ilgili bir çözümden söz eder ama sıcaklığın yüksek kalmasına neden olamaz."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-06", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-05"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nSea otters feed heavily on sea urchins, which in turn graze on kelp, a large seaweed that forms underwater forests. When sea otters were hunted almost to extinction for their fur in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, urchin populations exploded along the Pacific coast of North America. The urchins consumed so much kelp that vast forests disappeared, taking with them the fish and other species that depended on them. ----", o:["Sea otter fur is among the densest of any animal.","Kelp is also used as an ingredient in some foods and cosmetics.","Sea urchins are, therefore, considered a threatened species today.","Where otters have since been reintroduced, however, urchin numbers have dropped and kelp forests have begun to recover.","Fishing for sea urchins is banned in many countries."], a:3, e:"Paragraf su samurlarının yok olmasının zincirleme sonuçlarını anlatır; son adım olarak samurların geri dönüşüyle zincirin tersine işlediğini gösteren D gelir. C “therefore” ile bağlanıyor gibi görünse de paragrafta sayısı patladığı anlatılan deniz kestanelerini tehdit altında bir tür gibi gösterir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-07", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-03","reading-13"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n---- In this ancient method, farmers grow a different crop on the same field each season rather than planting the same one year after year. Because different plants take different nutrients from the soil, and some, such as beans and peas, even add nitrogen to it, the soil stays fertile for longer. The practice also disrupts the life cycles of pests that specialise in a single crop.", o:["One of the simplest ways to maintain soil health is crop rotation.","Beans and peas are rich sources of protein.","Pests cause billions of dollars of damage to crops every year.","Many farmers today rely heavily on chemical fertilisers.","Farmers in ancient times grew mainly wheat and barley."], a:0, e:"“In this ancient method” ifadesi ilk cümlede bir yöntemin adının geçmesini zorunlu kılar; bunu yalnızca A (crop rotation) sağlar. E “ancient” ve “farmers” sözcükleriyle bağlantılı görünür ama bir yöntemden söz etmez."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-08", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-06","reading-14"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nThe idea that handwashing could prevent disease was put forward by the Hungarian doctor Ignaz Semmelweis in the 1840s. He noticed that women giving birth in a ward run by doctors, who often came straight from performing autopsies, died far more often than those cared for by midwives. When he required doctors to wash their hands in a chlorine solution, the death rate fell dramatically. ---- It was only decades later, after Louis Pasteur's work on germs, that the importance of hygiene in hospitals became widely accepted.", o:["As a result, handwashing became standard practice in hospitals across Europe within a few months.","Midwives at that time received very little formal training.","Despite this striking result, many of his colleagues rejected his ideas, partly because he could not explain why handwashing worked.","Chlorine is still used today to disinfect drinking water.","Louis Pasteur was born in France in 1822."], a:2, e:"Ölüm oranının düşmesine rağmen hijyenin ancak on yıllar sonra kabul görmesi, “Despite this striking result … rejected” zıtlığıyla bağlanır. A “within a few months” diyerek “only decades later” ifadesiyle doğrudan çelişir; E ise yalnızca Pasteur adını tekrar eder."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-09", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-04","reading-15"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nMany companies now offer employees the option of working from home several days a week. Early concerns that productivity would fall have largely proved unfounded; some studies even report small gains. ---- These problems are particularly serious for newly hired staff, who have fewer chances to learn informally from more experienced colleagues.", o:["Office rents in large cities have fallen in recent years.","Therefore, most companies have decided to close their offices permanently.","Many employees use the time saved on commuting to exercise or to spend with their families.","Productivity is usually measured by the amount of work completed per hour.","Remote work, however, can weaken communication and make it harder to build trust within teams."], a:4, e:"Sonraki cümledeki “These problems” boşlukta sorunların sayılmasını gerektirir; “however” da önceki olumlu tabloyla karşıtlık kurar. C evden çalışmayla ilgilidir ama olumlu bir yön anlattığı için “These problems” göndermesini karşılamaz."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-10", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-06"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nBamboo is one of the fastest-growing plants on Earth; some species can grow nearly a metre in a single day. It is also remarkably strong for its weight, with a tensile strength comparable to that of some types of steel. For these reasons, builders in tropical regions have long used it for scaffolding, bridges and houses. ----", o:["Pandas feed almost entirely on bamboo leaves and shoots.","Today, engineers in other parts of the world are also becoming interested in bamboo as a sustainable alternative to conventional building materials.","Steel, however, was first produced in large quantities in the nineteenth century.","Bamboo, therefore, is rarely used in construction.","Tropical regions receive heavy rainfall for much of the year."], a:1, e:"Paragraf bambunun özelliklerinden yapı malzemesi olarak kullanımına ilerler; B bu kullanımın günümüzde yayıldığını söyleyerek son gelişmeyi sürdürür. D “therefore” ile bağlanıyor gibi görünse de önceki cümleyle çelişir; A ise yalnızca bambu kelimesini tekrar eder."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-11", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-13","w8-04"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nEconomists use the term \"opportunity cost\" to describe the value of the best alternative that is given up when a choice is made. ---- Similarly, a government that spends money on building a new motorway cannot use the same funds to improve hospitals or schools. Recognising such hidden costs, economists argue, leads to better decisions by both individuals and policymakers.", o:["The term was first used in the early twentieth century.","Many governments have reduced spending on motorways in recent years.","For example, a student who spends an evening at the cinema gives up the chance to use that time for studying or working.","Opportunity costs, therefore, are always measured in money.","Hospitals and schools are among the largest items of public spending."], a:2, e:"Sonraki cümledeki “Similarly” ondan önce benzer bir örnek verilmiş olmasını gerektirir; C bireysel düzeyde bir örnek sunar, ardından devlet örneği gelir. D “always … in money” diyerek zamanın da bir maliyet olabileceğini dışlar ve akışı bozar."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-12", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-03","w8-02"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n---- She discovered that DDT and other chemicals were accumulating in the food chain, killing birds and fish and threatening human health. Her book Silent Spring, published in 1962, caused a public outcry and is widely credited with inspiring the modern environmental movement. Within a decade, DDT had been banned for agricultural use in the United States.", o:["Pesticides are chemicals designed to kill insects that damage crops.","In the 1950s, the American biologist Rachel Carson began investigating the effects of widely used pesticides on wildlife.","Many birds migrate thousands of kilometres every year.","The environmental movement had already become powerful in the nineteenth century.","DDT was first synthesised in 1874 by an Austrian chemist."], a:1, e:"İkinci cümledeki “She” zamiri ilk cümlede bir kadının tanıtılmasını gerektirir; bunu yalnızca B sağlar. E DDT'den söz ettiği için bağlantılı görünür ama “She” göndermesini karşılamaz; A da yalnızca genel bir tanım verir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-13", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-14","w8-06"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nFever is often seen simply as an unpleasant symptom to be treated as quickly as possible. In fact, a raised body temperature is one of the body's defences against infection: many bacteria and viruses reproduce less efficiently at higher temperatures, and some immune cells work faster. ---- A very high fever, though, can be dangerous, especially for young children, and should always be taken seriously.", o:["Therefore, fever should never be treated under any circumstances.","Bacteria were first observed under a microscope in the seventeenth century.","Young children catch colds more often than adults.","As a result, fever always indicates a serious illness.","For this reason, some doctors advise against automatically reducing a mild fever."], a:4, e:"Ateşin savunma işlevi görmesi, hafif ateşin hemen düşürülmemesi tavsiyesine yol açar; sonraki cümledeki “though” da bu tavsiyeye “çok yüksek ateş ise tehlikelidir” diye sınır koyar. A “never … under any circumstances” diyerek bu sınırlamayla çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-14", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-15","w8-01"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nUntil the eighteenth century, most people in Europe lived in the countryside and worked on the land. The invention of machines such as the spinning jenny and the steam engine then made it possible to produce goods in factories on a large scale. ---- This shift created crowded, unhealthy cities, but it also laid the foundations for the rising living standards of later generations.", o:["Millions of people consequently left their villages to find work in rapidly growing industrial towns.","The steam engine was later used to power ships and locomotives.","Farming methods in the eighteenth century had changed little since the Middle Ages.","Factories, however, were rarely built near cities.","Living standards fell steadily throughout the following two centuries."], a:0, e:"“This shift created crowded … cities” ifadesi, köyden kente göçü anlatan bir cümleye gönderme yapar; bunu A karşılar. B buhar makinesi kelimesini tekrar eder ama kentlerin kalabalıklaşmasına geçişi sağlamaz; E ise son cümleyle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-15", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-04"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nOver the past two decades, the price of genome sequencing has fallen dramatically, from nearly three billion dollars for the first human genome to a few hundred dollars today. As a result, doctors can increasingly use genetic information to choose treatments suited to individual patients, an approach known as personalised medicine. Certain cancer drugs, for example, are now prescribed only to patients whose tumours carry specific genetic mutations. ----", o:["The first human genome was sequenced by an international team of scientists.","Genetic information, therefore, has become useless in treating cancer.","Most cancers are caused by poor diet and lack of exercise.","Such targeted treatments can be more effective and cause fewer side effects than conventional therapies.","Doctors have always been reluctant to prescribe new drugs."], a:3, e:"“Such targeted treatments” son cümledeki genetik mutasyona göre verilen ilaçlara gönderme yapar ve paragrafı bu yaklaşımın yararıyla bitirir. A ilk genomdan söz ettiği için ilgili görünür ama paragrafın son gelişmesini sürdürmez; B ise örnekle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-16", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-05","reading-14"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nMany large Asian rivers, including the Ganges and the Indus, are fed partly by meltwater from Himalayan glaciers. During hot, dry months, this meltwater keeps the rivers flowing when rainfall is scarce. ---- Hundreds of millions of people living downstream could therefore face serious water shortages later this century.", o:["The Ganges is considered a sacred river by many Hindus.","Some Himalayan peaks are more than eight thousand metres high.","Rainfall in the region is heaviest during the summer monsoon.","As a result, river levels have been rising steadily for the past hundred years.","However, rising temperatures are causing many of these glaciers to shrink at an accelerating rate."], a:4, e:"“could therefore face serious water shortages” sonucu, buzulların küçüldüğünü söyleyen bir neden cümlesi gerektirir; “However” da önceki olumlu işlevle karşıtlık kurar. D “As a result” ile bağlanır gibi görünür ama su kıtlığı sonucuna gerekçe oluşturmaz, aksine onunla çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-17", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-03","reading-16"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n---- These tiny devices, now found in everything from washing machines to cars, perform millions of calculations per second while consuming very little power. Their low cost is the result of mass production: billions are manufactured every year using techniques that etch circuits onto thin slices of silicon.", o:["Silicon is the second most abundant element in the Earth's crust.","Washing machines have become much more efficient in recent decades.","Cars today produce far less pollution than they did in the 1970s.","Microchips have become an almost invisible but essential part of modern life.","These calculations, however, require large amounts of electricity."], a:3, e:"“These tiny devices” ilk cümlede küçük bir aygıtın adının geçmesini gerektirir; bunu yalnızca D (microchips) sağlar. A silikon kelimesini, B ve C ise örnek olarak geçen makineleri tekrar eder ama göndermeyi karşılamaz; E sonraki cümledeki “very little power” ile çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-18", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-02","reading-13"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nThe Great Wall of China is often described as a single continuous structure. ---- Many of these were built of rammed earth rather than stone, and the brick sections most familiar to tourists date mainly from the Ming dynasty, between the fourteenth and seventeenth centuries. Moreover, the popular claim that the wall can be seen with the naked eye from space has been rejected by astronauts.", o:["It attracts millions of tourists every year.","In reality, it is a series of walls built and rebuilt by different dynasties over roughly two thousand years.","The Ming dynasty is famous for its blue-and-white porcelain.","Astronauts have taken many photographs of China from space.","It was, therefore, completed within a single century."], a:1, e:"Sonraki cümledeki “Many of these” çoğul bir şeye (farklı duvarlara) gönderme yapar; B yaygın “tek yapı” görüşünü “In reality” ile düzeltir. A turistlerden söz ettiği için ilgili görünür ama “these” göndermesini karşılamaz; E ise Ming dönemine ait bölümlerle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-19", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-13","w8-06"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nTea was first drunk in China as a medicine more than two thousand years ago. By the seventeenth century, Dutch and English merchants had brought it to Europe, where it quickly became fashionable among the wealthy. ---- In Britain, for instance, the demand for tea helped drive the expansion of trade with Asia, and disputes over tea taxes contributed to the American colonists' revolt against British rule.", o:["Tea contains less caffeine than the same amount of coffee.","Green and black tea are made from the leaves of the same plant.","Its impact, however, soon extended well beyond people's drinking habits to trade and even politics.","Coffee houses were also popular meeting places in seventeenth-century London.","Tea was, therefore, rarely drunk outside China until the twentieth century."], a:2, e:"Sonraki cümle “for instance” ile ticaret ve siyasetten örnek verir; bu örnekler çayın etkisinin içecek alışkanlığının ötesine geçtiğini söyleyen C'ye bağlanır. D aynı dönemden ve ülkeden söz eder ama sonraki örnekleri açıklamaz; E ise ikinci cümleyle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-20", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-05"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nBats find their way in the dark by emitting high-pitched calls and listening to the echoes that bounce back from objects around them. This ability, called echolocation, is so precise that some species can detect an insect as thin as a human hair. Engineers have studied the phenomenon closely, and similar principles are used in the sonar systems of ships. ----", o:["More recently, researchers have begun developing echolocation-based devices that help blind people detect obstacles in their path.","Bats are the only mammals capable of true flight.","Ships, therefore, no longer need any other navigation equipment.","Many bat species hibernate during the winter months.","Insects, however, are an important food source for many birds."], a:0, e:"Paragraf yankıyla yön bulmanın teknolojiye uygulanmasıyla ilerler; A “More recently” ile bu uygulamanın yeni bir örneğini ekleyerek son gelişmeyi sürdürür. C “therefore” ile bağlanır gibi görünür ama abartılı ve dayanaksız bir sonuç çıkarır; B ve D yalnızca yarasalar hakkında genel bilgi verir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-21", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-04","reading-15"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nResearchers studying happiness have long noticed a puzzling pattern. As a country grows richer, its citizens do not necessarily become more satisfied with their lives. ---- This finding suggests that people judge their own well-being largely by comparing themselves with others rather than by absolute standards.", o:["Within any given country at a particular time, however, people who earn more than those around them tend to report greater happiness.","Many countries have become much richer since the Second World War.","Happiness is usually measured through surveys in which people rate their lives on a scale.","Therefore, richer people are always happier than poorer ones.","Some economists argue that governments should focus solely on economic growth."], a:0, e:"“This finding” kişilerin kendilerini başkalarıyla kıyasladığını gösteren bir bulguya gönderme yapar; A çevresindekilerden fazla kazananın daha mutlu olduğunu söyleyerek bunu karşılar. C araştırma yöntemini anlatır ama “karşılaştırma” fikrini içeren bir bulgu sunmaz; D ise “always” diyerek abartır."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-22", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-03","reading-13"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n---- The name, however, is misleading. It was coined by Renaissance scholars who regarded the centuries after the fall of Rome as a time of cultural decline. Modern historians largely reject this view, pointing out that the period saw important advances in agriculture, architecture and learning.", o:["The Western Roman Empire collapsed in the late fifth century.","Renaissance art was greatly influenced by classical Greek and Roman models.","The early medieval period in Europe is still sometimes referred to as the \"Dark Ages\".","Agriculture was the main occupation of most people in medieval Europe.","Modern historians have written many books about the Renaissance."], a:2, e:"İkinci cümledeki “The name” ilk cümlede bir adın verilmesini gerektirir; C “Dark Ages” adını tanıtır ve “misleading” yargısı bu olumsuz adla anlam kazanır. A Roma'nın çöküşünden söz ettiği için ilgili görünür ama bir addan bahsetmez."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-23", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-14","w8-02"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nNuclear power plants produce very little carbon dioxide during operation, which makes them attractive to countries trying to meet climate targets. ---- Critics, though, point to the high cost and long construction times of new plants, as well as the unresolved problem of storing radioactive waste safely for thousands of years.", o:["Nuclear energy is therefore the cheapest and quickest way to reduce emissions.","Radioactive waste was first produced in the 1940s.","Some countries have large reserves of coal and natural gas.","They also provide a stable supply of electricity regardless of weather conditions, unlike solar and wind power.","Climate targets were agreed by many countries in Paris in 2015."], a:3, e:"Boşluk, nükleer enerjinin artılarını sürdüren bir cümle gerektirir; “Critics, though” ile ardından eksiler gelir. A da olumlu görünür ama “cheapest and quickest” ifadesi eleştirmenlerin “high cost and long construction times” itirazıyla doğrudan çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-24", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-05"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nTraditionally, the success of a school has been judged mainly by its students' examination results. Yet a growing number of educators argue that this narrow focus ignores skills that are equally important in adult life, such as cooperation, creativity and the ability to cope with failure. Some countries have therefore begun to include measures of students' well-being and social skills in school evaluations. ----", o:["Examinations were first used to select government officials in ancient China.","Supporters of this approach believe it will encourage schools to develop the whole child rather than simply teach to the test.","As a result, examination results are no longer recorded anywhere.","Creativity is difficult to define precisely.","Many adults find it hard to cope with failure at work."], a:1, e:"“this approach” son cümledeki yeni değerlendirme yöntemine gönderme yapar ve paragrafı savunucuların beklentisiyle bitirir. C “As a result” ile bağlanır gibi görünse de “no longer recorded anywhere” diyerek abartır; D ve E ise paragrafta geçen kelimeleri tekrar eder ama akışı ilerletmez."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-25", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-13","w8-02"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nInvasive species are plants or animals introduced, often accidentally, into regions where they did not previously exist. Without the predators and diseases that kept their numbers in check at home, they can spread rapidly and push out native species. ---- Within a few decades, it had wiped out most of the island's native forest birds.", o:["Many islands have unique species that are found nowhere else on Earth.","Some invasive species, however, have proved useful to farmers.","Governments spend large sums trying to control invasive plants.","Native species, therefore, usually adapt quickly to newcomers.","The brown tree snake, for example, reached the Pacific island of Guam in cargo shipments after the Second World War."], a:4, e:"Sonraki cümledeki tekil “it” ve “the island's” ifadeleri, boşlukta belirli bir türün belirli bir adaya gelişinin anlatılmasını gerektirir; bunu E sağlar. A adalardan söz eder ama “it” zamirinin göndermesini karşılamaz; D ise önceki cümleyle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-26", sub:"rd-completion", from:["w8-01","reading-15"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nMost animals age steadily and eventually die. A small jellyfish known as Turritopsis dohrnii, however, has an extraordinary ability. ---- In theory, this process could be repeated indefinitely, which is why the species is sometimes described as \"biologically immortal\".", o:["Jellyfish have existed in the oceans for more than five hundred million years.","When it is injured or stressed, it can transform its adult cells back into those of an earlier, juvenile stage and begin its life cycle again.","Most jellyfish species live for only a few months.","In practice, however, it dies of old age like other animals.","Its sting is dangerous to swimmers in warm waters."], a:1, e:"“this process could be repeated” ifadesi, boşlukta tekrarlanabilir bir sürecin anlatılmasını gerektirir; B bu olağanüstü yeteneği tanımlar. D “however” ile bağlanır gibi görünse de “extraordinary ability” ve “biologically immortal” ifadeleriyle çelişir."},
  {id:"r-rd-completion-27", sub:"rd-completion", from:["reading-16","w8-06"], q:"Parçada boş bırakılan yere, parçanın anlam bütünlüğünü sağlamak için getirilebilecek cümleyi bulunuz.\n\nEsperanto was created in the 1880s by L. L. Zamenhof, who hoped that a simple, neutral international language would promote peace between nations. Its grammar is extremely regular, and its vocabulary draws mainly on European languages, making it relatively easy for many learners to acquire. Although it attracted enthusiastic supporters and is still spoken by perhaps a few hundred thousand people, it never achieved the global role its creator had imagined. ----", o:["Zamenhof was an eye doctor by profession.","Therefore, Esperanto is now the official language of several countries.","Its grammar, moreover, is more complicated than that of most natural languages.","European languages share many words of Latin origin.","Instead, English has increasingly come to serve as the world's common language."], a:4, e:"Son cümle Esperanto'nun küresel role ulaşamadığını söyler; E “Instead” ile bu rolü İngilizcenin üstlendiğini belirterek paragrafı mantıklı biçimde bitirir. B “Therefore” ile bağlanır gibi görünür ama önceki cümleyle çelişir; C de “extremely regular” ifadesine ters düşer."},

  /* ---------- rd-irrelevant ---------- */
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-01", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-17","w8-11"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Mangrove forests grow along tropical coastlines where land meets the sea. (II) Their dense, tangled roots slow down waves and help protect coastal communities from storms and erosion. (III) Many tropical beaches have become popular destinations for international tourists. (IV) Mangroves also store large amounts of carbon in their waterlogged soils, often more per hectare than tropical rainforests. (V) Despite these benefits, more than a third of the world's mangroves have been cleared, mainly for shrimp farms and coastal development.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragrafın konusu mangrov ormanlarının yararları ve yok edilmesidir; III ise tropik plajların turizmine geçer. “tropical” ve kıyı teması ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; V ise “these benefits” ile II ve IV'ü toparlar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-02", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-18","w8-07"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Many microscopic organisms play a vital role in breaking down dead plant material in the soil. (II) Tardigrades, tiny animals less than a millimetre long, are among the toughest creatures known to science. (III) They can survive being frozen to almost absolute zero, heated above the boiling point of water and exposed to intense radiation. (IV) In 2007, some even survived ten days in the vacuum of outer space. (V) Their secret appears to be a state called cryptobiosis, in which they lose nearly all their body water and shut down their metabolism almost entirely.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:0, e:"Paragraf II'den itibaren su ayılarının (tardigrade) olağanüstü dayanıklılığını anlatır; I ise topraktaki mikroorganizmaların ayrıştırma işlevinden söz eder ve sonraki cümlelerle hiçbir göndermeyle bağlanmaz. I çıkarıldığında paragraf II ile sorunsuz başlar; III'teki “They” de II'deki tardigradelere gönderme yapar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-03", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-11","reading-19"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The Dead Sea, located between Jordan and Israel, is one of the saltiest bodies of water on Earth. (II) Its salt concentration is so high that swimmers float effortlessly on the surface. (III) However, the sea is shrinking rapidly, with its level falling by more than a metre each year. (IV) Salt was so valuable in the ancient world that Roman soldiers were sometimes paid partly in it. (V) The main cause of this decline is the diversion of water from the Jordan River, which once supplied most of the sea's inflow.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragraf Lut Gölü'nü ve küçülmesinin nedenini anlatır; IV, “salt” kelimesinden yola çıkarak antik dünyada tuzun değerine sapar. V'teki “this decline” doğrudan III'e bağlandığından IV'ün araya sonradan girdiği anlaşılır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-04", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-09","reading-18"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The Black Death, which swept across Europe between 1347 and 1351, killed perhaps a third of the continent's population. (II) The resulting shortage of workers gave surviving peasants greater bargaining power. (III) In many regions, wages rose and labourers were able to demand better conditions from landowners. (IV) Some historians therefore argue that the plague helped to weaken the feudal system in western Europe. (V) Modern vaccines have made many once-deadly infectious diseases far less common.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:4, e:"Paragraf Kara Ölüm'ün Avrupa'daki toplumsal ve ekonomik sonuçlarını anlatır; V ise günümüz aşılarına geçerek konudan kopar. Salgın hastalık teması ortak olduğu için V ilgili görünür; IV ise “therefore” ile önceki sonuçları toparlar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-05", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-12","w8-08"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Ada Lovelace, the daughter of the poet Lord Byron, is often described as the first computer programmer. (II) Lord Byron was one of the leading figures of the Romantic movement in English literature. (III) In the 1840s, she wrote detailed notes on Charles Babbage's design for a mechanical computing machine known as the Analytical Engine. (IV) These notes included a step-by-step method for calculating a sequence of numbers, now regarded as the first computer program. (V) She also foresaw that such machines might one day process not only numbers but also music and images.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:1, e:"Paragraf Ada Lovelace'in bilgisayar tarihindeki yerini anlatır; II ise babası Lord Byron'ın edebi konumuna geçer. III'teki “she” zamiri doğrudan I'deki Ada Lovelace'e bağlandığından II'nin araya girdiği açıktır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-06", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-20","w8-08"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Many plants have developed clever ways of defending themselves against the animals that eat them. (II) Gardening has become one of the most popular hobbies among retired people in Europe. (III) One example is the acacia tree, which houses colonies of aggressive ants that attack any animal trying to feed on its leaves. (IV) Other plants, such as tomatoes, release chemical signals when damaged, prompting nearby plants to produce substances that make their leaves less tasty. (V) These strategies show that plants are far from passive victims in their relationships with plant-eating animals.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:1, e:"III'teki “One example” doğrudan I'deki bitkilerin savunma yollarına örnek verir; aradaki II (bahçecilik hobisi) bu bağı koparır. IV “Other plants” ile örnekleri sürdürür, V ise “These strategies” ile toparlar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-07", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-10","reading-20"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Inflation refers to a general increase in prices across an economy over time. (II) Moderate inflation is usually considered normal, and many central banks aim to keep it at around two percent a year. (III) When inflation rises too quickly, however, it reduces the purchasing power of wages and savings. (IV) Many central bank buildings are architecturally impressive structures located in capital cities. (V) People on fixed incomes, such as pensioners, are often hit hardest by such price increases.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragraf enflasyonun tanımını ve alım gücüne etkisini anlatır; IV, II'deki “central banks” ifadesinden yola çıkarak merkez bankası binalarına sapar. V'teki “such price increases” III'e bağlanarak akışı sürdürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-08", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-18","w8-07"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Cataracts, a clouding of the lens of the eye, can now be treated with a short and safe surgical operation. (II) Braille, a system of raised dots that can be read by touch, was developed in the 1820s by Louis Braille, a young Frenchman who had lost his sight in childhood. (III) He based his system on a method of \"night writing\" designed to allow soldiers to communicate in the dark. (IV) Each Braille character is formed from a cell of up to six dots arranged in two columns. (V) Today, the system has been adapted to almost every written language and is also used for mathematics and music.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:0, e:"Paragraf II'den itibaren Braille alfabesinin doğuşunu ve yapısını anlatır; I ise katarakt ameliyatından söz eder. Görme konusu ortak olduğu için I giriş cümlesi gibi görünür, ama hiçbir cümle ona gönderme yapmaz; III'teki “He” ise II'deki Louis Braille'e bağlanır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-09", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-10","reading-17"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Vertical farming involves growing crops in stacked layers inside buildings, often in the middle of cities. (II) Because the plants are grown under LED lights in carefully controlled conditions, they can be harvested all year round without pesticides. (III) Skyscrapers first appeared in Chicago and New York at the end of the nineteenth century. (IV) The method also uses up to ninety-five percent less water than conventional agriculture, since water is recycled within the system. (V) High energy costs, however, mean that vertical farms are currently profitable only for a limited range of crops, such as leafy greens and herbs.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragraf dikey tarımın avantajlarını ve sınırlılığını anlatır; III, “binalar” fikrinden yola çıkarak gökdelenlerin tarihine sapar. IV'teki “The method also” ifadesi II'deki avantajları sürdürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-10", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-09","w8-12"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The first successful human heart transplant was performed by the South African surgeon Christiaan Barnard in 1967. (II) Although the patient survived for only eighteen days, the operation attracted worldwide attention. (III) Early results were disappointing, as most recipients died soon afterwards because their immune systems rejected the new organ. (IV) The introduction of the drug cyclosporine in the 1980s greatly reduced this problem, and survival rates rose sharply. (V) South Africa is known for its rich wildlife, which attracts visitors from around the world.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:4, e:"Paragraf kalp naklinin tarihini ve organ reddi sorununun çözülmesini anlatır; V ise I'deki “South African” ifadesinden yola çıkarak Güney Afrika'nın vahşi yaşamına sapar. IV'teki “this problem” III'teki reddi karşıladığından akışa uygundur."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-11", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-11","reading-18"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Coffee originated in the highlands of Ethiopia, where, according to legend, a goat herder noticed his animals becoming unusually energetic after eating the berries of a certain shrub. (II) By the fifteenth century, coffee was being cultivated in Yemen and drunk in Sufi monasteries to help worshippers stay awake during night prayers. (III) From there, it spread rapidly to Cairo, Istanbul and other cities of the Ottoman Empire, where the first coffee houses opened. (IV) In the seventeenth century, European traders brought the drink to Venice, London and Paris. (V) Goats are able to digest many plants that other animals cannot eat.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:4, e:"Paragraf kahvenin Etiyopya'dan Avrupa'ya yayılışını kronolojik olarak anlatır; V ise I'deki efsanede geçen keçilerden yola çıkarak keçilerin sindirimine sapar. III'teki “From there” II'ye bağlandığından akışa uygundur."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-12", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-19","w8-08"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Antibiotic resistance occurs when bacteria evolve so that the drugs designed to kill them no longer work. (II) The overuse of antibiotics in both medicine and livestock farming has greatly accelerated this process. (III) Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin in 1928 after noticing that mould had killed bacteria in one of his laboratory dishes. (IV) As a result, infections that were once easily treated, such as pneumonia and tuberculosis, are becoming harder to cure. (V) Experts warn that without new drugs and more careful use of existing ones, routine surgery could become far more dangerous in the future.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragraf antibiyotik direncinin nedenini ve sonuçlarını anlatır; III penisilinin keşif tarihine sapar. “antibiotics” ve “bacteria” kelimeleri ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; IV'teki “As a result” ise doğrudan II'deki aşırı kullanıma bağlanır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-13", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-07","reading-17"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Urban trees provide far more than shade and beauty. (II) The oak is one of the longest-living trees in Europe, with some specimens thought to be more than a thousand years old. (III) Studies show that tree-lined streets can be several degrees cooler in summer than streets without trees, reducing the need for air conditioning. (IV) Trees also absorb rainwater, lowering the risk of flooding during heavy storms. (V) In addition, research suggests that people living near green spaces report lower levels of stress.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:1, e:"Paragrafın konusu kent ağaçlarının sağladığı yararlardır; II ise meşe ağacının ömrüne geçer. “trees” kelimesi ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; III, IV ve V ise I'deki “far more than shade and beauty” iddiasını örneklerle destekler."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-14", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-18","w8-12"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The Inca Empire, which stretched along the Andes in South America, had no system of writing in the usual sense. (II) Instead, officials recorded information using quipus, bundles of knotted cords made of cotton or llama wool. (III) The type, position and colour of the knots represented numbers and possibly other kinds of data, such as census results and tax records. (IV) The Incas grew potatoes and maize on terraces cut into steep mountain slopes. (V) Although hundreds of quipus survive, scholars are still trying to determine whether any of them record words as well as numbers.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragraf İnkaların düğümlü iplerle (quipu) kayıt tutma sistemini anlatır; IV ise aynı uygarlığın tarımına geçer. Aynı uygarlıktan söz ettiği için çeldiricidir; V ise quipu konusuna geri döner."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-15", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-20","w8-10"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The New York Stock Exchange, founded in 1792, is the largest stock exchange in the world by market value. (II) Crowdfunding has become an increasingly popular way for individuals and small businesses to raise money for new projects. (III) Through online platforms, creators present their ideas and ask large numbers of people to contribute small amounts. (IV) In return, supporters often receive early access to the product or a small reward. (V) Critics warn, however, that many crowdfunded projects are delivered late or never at all, leaving backers with little legal protection.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:0, e:"Paragraf II'den itibaren kitlesel fonlamayı (crowdfunding), işleyişini ve risklerini anlatır; I ise New York Borsası'nın büyüklüğünden söz eder ve sonraki cümlelerin hiçbiri ona gönderme yapmaz. Finans alanı ortak olduğu için I giriş cümlesi gibi görünse de konu II'de başlar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-16", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-11","reading-17"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Loneliness is increasingly recognised as a serious public health issue. (II) Research indicates that chronic loneliness raises the risk of heart disease, depression and early death to a degree comparable with smoking. (III) Older people are particularly vulnerable, as retirement and the loss of partners and friends can shrink their social networks. (IV) Smoking rates have fallen significantly in most developed countries since the 1970s. (V) In response to such concerns, the United Kingdom appointed a minister for loneliness in 2018 to coordinate efforts to tackle the problem.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragrafın konusu yalnızlığın bir halk sağlığı sorunu olmasıdır; IV, II'deki “smoking” karşılaştırmasından yola çıkarak sigara içme oranlarına sapar. V'teki “such concerns” ve “the problem” yalnızlık konusuna geri döner."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-17", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-09","reading-18"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Nomadic peoples of the Eurasian steppe were among the first to domesticate the horse, around five thousand years ago. (II) Horses allowed them to travel long distances quickly and to herd large numbers of animals. (III) Later, mounted archers gave steppe peoples such as the Mongols a decisive military advantage over settled societies. (IV) Under Genghis Khan and his successors, these horsemen built the largest land empire in history. (V) Horse racing remains a popular sport in many countries, attracting large sums in betting.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:4, e:"Paragraf atın bozkır halklarının tarihindeki rolünü anlatır; V ise günümüz at yarışlarına geçer. “horse” kelimesi ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; IV'teki “these horsemen” ise III'e bağlanarak akışı sürdürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-18", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-19","w8-08"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Glass frogs, found in the rainforests of Central and South America, have translucent skin on their undersides. (II) Through it, observers can see their hearts, livers and other internal organs. (III) Rainforests are home to more than half of the world's plant and animal species. (IV) Researchers recently discovered that when these frogs sleep, they hide most of their red blood cells in their livers, making their bodies almost completely transparent. (V) This ability helps them avoid predators by allowing them to blend in with the leaves on which they rest.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragraf cam kurbağalarının saydamlığını ve bunun yararını anlatır; III ise yağmur ormanlarının biyolojik çeşitliliğine sapar. I'de geçen “rainforests” kelimesi yüzünden ilgili görünür; IV'teki “these frogs” ise II'ye bağlanır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-19", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-07","reading-18"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Venus, the planet closest in size to Earth, is covered by thick clouds of sulphuric acid. (II) Since the 1970s, a series of robotic missions has landed on the surface of Mars to study its geology and climate. (III) Rovers such as Curiosity and Perseverance have found evidence that liquid water once flowed across the planet's surface. (IV) They have also detected organic molecules in Martian rocks, although these could have been formed by non-biological processes. (V) Scientists hope that samples collected by these rovers will eventually be returned to Earth for more detailed analysis.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:0, e:"Paragraf II'den itibaren Mars'a gönderilen robotik görevleri ve bulgularını anlatır; I ise Venüs'ün atmosferinden söz eder ve hiçbir cümle ona bağlanmaz. Gezegen teması ortak olduğu için I giriş gibi görünse de III'teki “the planet” Mars'a, IV'teki “They” de gezginlere gönderme yapar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-20", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-08","w8-12"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Octopuses are widely regarded as the most intelligent invertebrates. (II) Squid are commonly served as food in Mediterranean and East Asian cuisines. (III) In laboratory studies, octopuses have learned to open screw-top jars and find their way through simple mazes. (IV) Some have even been observed escaping from their tanks at night, raiding neighbouring tanks for food and then returning. (V) Remarkably, about two-thirds of an octopus's neurons are located not in its brain but in its arms.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:1, e:"Paragraf ahtapotların zekâsını anlatır; II ise kalamarın mutfaklardaki yerine geçer. Benzer bir deniz canlısından söz ettiği için çeldiricidir; III ve IV ise I'deki zekâ iddiasını örneklerle destekler."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-21", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-18","reading-20"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Norway is one of the world's largest exporters of oil and natural gas. (II) Deep inside a mountain on the Arctic island of Svalbard lies a vault designed to protect the world's crop diversity. (III) It holds more than a million seed samples sent by gene banks from almost every country. (IV) The permanently frozen ground around it keeps the seeds cold even if the electricity supply fails. (V) In 2015, researchers withdrew seeds from the vault for the first time to replace collections lost during the war in Syria.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:0, e:"Paragraf II'den itibaren Svalbard'daki küresel tohum deposunu anlatır; I ise Norveç'in petrol ve doğalgaz ihracatından söz eder. Svalbard Norveç'e ait olduğu için I ilgili görünür, ama III'teki “It” ve IV'teki “around it” II'deki depoya gönderme yapar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-22", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-07","reading-20"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Carbon taxes put a price on greenhouse gas emissions in order to encourage businesses and households to pollute less. (II) Carbon is found in all known living organisms. (III) Economists generally favour this approach because it allows people to decide for themselves the cheapest way to cut emissions. (IV) Critics argue, however, that such taxes can hit low-income households hardest, since they spend a larger share of their income on energy. (V) To address this concern, some governments return the revenue to citizens in the form of regular payments.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:1, e:"Paragraf karbon vergisinin mantığını, eleştirilerini ve çözümünü anlatır; II ise “carbon” kelimesinden yola çıkarak canlılardaki karbona sapar. III'teki “this approach” doğrudan I'deki vergiye gönderme yaptığından II'nin araya girdiği açıktır."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-23", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-09","w8-12"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) The Hanseatic League was a powerful alliance of merchant towns that dominated trade in northern Europe from the thirteenth to the fifteenth century. (II) Its members, including Lübeck, Hamburg and Bergen, cooperated to protect their ships from pirates and to secure trading privileges abroad. (III) Goods such as timber, furs, grain and salted fish passed through its network of ports. (IV) The rise of powerful national states and new Atlantic trade routes eventually led to its decline. (V) Hamburg today has one of the busiest container ports in Europe.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:4, e:"Paragraf Hansa Birliği'nin yükselişini, ticaretini ve çöküşünü anlatır; V ise II'de geçen Hamburg'un günümüzdeki limanına sapar. IV birliğin çöküşünü anlatarak konuyu tamamlar."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-24", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-11","reading-17"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Dyslexia is a learning difference that mainly affects the ability to read and spell accurately. (II) It is not related to intelligence, and many people with dyslexia excel in areas such as problem-solving and creative thinking. (III) Reading for pleasure has declined among teenagers in many countries over the past two decades. (IV) Brain imaging studies suggest that people with dyslexia process the sounds of language differently. (V) With early identification and appropriate teaching methods, most children with dyslexia can learn to read well.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragrafın konusu disleksidir; III ise gençlerde keyif için okumanın azalmasına geçer. “reading” kelimesi ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; IV ve V ise disleksinin nedenlerini ve desteklenmesini anlatarak konuyu sürdürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-25", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-10","reading-19"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Desalination is the process of removing salt from seawater to produce fresh water. (II) It has become an essential source of drinking water in dry regions such as the Middle East. (III) Most modern plants use a method called reverse osmosis, in which seawater is forced through fine membranes at high pressure. (IV) Seawater contains small amounts of gold, although extracting it is not economically worthwhile. (V) The process consumes large amounts of energy, however, and the concentrated salty waste it produces can harm marine life when released back into the sea.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragraf tuzdan arındırmanın işleyişini ve sakıncalarını anlatır; IV “seawater” kelimesinden yola çıkarak deniz suyundaki altına sapar. V'teki “The process” III'teki yönteme bağlanarak konuyu sürdürür."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-26", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["reading-18","w8-12"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) Stonehenge, the prehistoric monument in southern England, was built in several stages between about 3000 and 1500 BCE. (II) Some of its smaller stones, known as bluestones, were transported from Wales, more than two hundred kilometres away. (III) Southern England has a mild climate, with relatively warm summers and cool, wet winters. (IV) The monument's main axis is aligned with the sunrise at the summer solstice, suggesting that it had a ceremonial or astronomical purpose. (V) Excavations nearby have also revealed the remains of a large settlement that may have housed the people who built it.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:2, e:"Paragraf Stonehenge'in yapımını, amacını ve çevresindeki buluntuları anlatır; III ise I'de geçen güney İngiltere'nin iklimine sapar. IV'teki “The monument's” ifadesi anıta geri döndüğünden akışa uygundur."},
  {id:"r-rd-irrelevant-27", sub:"rd-irrelevant", from:["w8-07","w8-11"], q:"Aşağıdaki parçada anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümleyi bulunuz.\n\n(I) A digital detox is a period during which people voluntarily stop using smartphones, computers and social media. (II) Supporters claim that such breaks can improve sleep, concentration and face-to-face relationships. (III) Some hotels and holiday resorts now even offer special packages in which guests hand over their devices on arrival. (IV) The first mobile phone with a touchscreen was introduced in the 1990s. (V) However, research on the long-term benefits of digital detox remains limited, and results so far have been mixed.", o:["I","II","III","IV","V"], a:3, e:"Paragraf dijital detoksu, yaygınlaşmasını ve kanıtların sınırlılığını anlatır; IV ise dokunmatik ekranlı telefonun tarihine sapar. Teknoloji teması ortak olduğu için ilgili görünür; V'teki “However” ise II'deki iddialara karşı çıkarak konuyu sürdürür."}
);
